  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Nightshelf crystallographer and practitioner of the ☽'glacial Crystalline~ Spiral — the fracture-magic developed by Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss that traps moments in ice at the cost of the caster's own memory. Mairae~ emerged from the Drowned Ledge during the Great Thaw, one of the survivors who sealed the upper tunnels and fled when the deepest shaft breached seawater. She learned to bend aurora-light through ice in configurations that, by any informed assessment of the Spiral's tolerances, should have killed her. That she survived is less a testament to skill than to whatever quality allows certain penguins to absorb punishment the discipline was not designed to inflict.
    
    Her flippers bear the white-scar tracery of frostburn — the consequence of working glacial spirals without proper shielding, a mistake she made once. Her left flipper aches in patterns she will not describe; she and her former teacher Keeper Hollows, a Nightshelf mentor now isolated at the sealed entrance to the Drowned Ledge, share the affliction and call it "the old trouble." She wears charcoal wraps layered thick enough to muffle sound, a hooded cloak threaded with bioluminescent script legible only to the dead, and an amulet of ancestor-bone recovered from the Drowned Ledge whose specific significance she has never disclosed.
    
    ## Work Against Corruption
    
    Mairae~'s aurora-crystals occasionally hold colors she has not catalogued, illuminating structures in the ice she does not believe were always present. This detail appears in every account and is never explained.
    
    She spent three seasons performing sanctification rites at Scar☽ Lucamlinaecius, the deep-carved depot beneath ☽'scar Ramtatus~, burning corruption back from the Marker's foundations. The taint retreated to sealed passages and crept back. She subsequently attempted a cleansing of the Glow-Fissure, one of the Berg's primary corruption sources, but no guild, Fire Keeper, or parliament body would provide escort. Only the Midnight Claws — the Nightshelf enforcement organization later dissolved by the Shadow Parliament for thirty winters of unsanctioned governance — agreed to accompany her. The corruption returned afterward. The pattern is consistent across every sanctification effort I have reviewed: temporary suppression, institutional indifference, and eventual reversion. Mairae~'s failure was not exceptional. It was structural.
    
    She continues sending fire-cores to Hollows through indebted couriers when his supply runs thin.
    
    ## Retenusus and the Shawl☽ Sun
    
    ☽'Retenusus the Undimmed, Dominus — a Nightshelf master of three disciplines — walked beside Mairae~ through the Faction Wars and the Clever Ice Age. She described their shared experience, in a phrase the chronicles preserved, as "stupidity and cowardice and the slow knowledge that one of them would not come back." Retenusus learned the Shawl of the Sun, a forbidden technique that burns corrupted memories from ice at the cost of the practitioner's own. The memory-burning consumed him. He forgot her face entirely before the season turned. Whether that loss was the fracture between them or its final expression, she will not confirm.
    
    ## Memorial and Aftermath
    
    The Drowned Ledge memorial stands at the colony's highest point. Mairae~'s name is carved into it alongside those she could not save. She once visited only in absolute darkness, setting down two fire-cores and leaving them burning until they guttered out. She eventually stopped going.
    
    Her fire-core hammer — its head cracked, its charge dimmed to a faint pulse — was left at the Drowned Ledge, where it is governed by Umbra∴im, the memorial rule that forbids its removal or repair. Successive generations are bound to witness what her hands wrought and failed to prevent. Penguins in the Frozen Peace still step aside when she moves through the tunnels — not from reverence, but from the sense that she carries something that might shatter if they stood too close.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771580642374_0", anchor: "by any informed assessment of the Spiral's tolerances, should have killed her", text: "Whose assessment? The tolerances are extrapolated from a discipline that, as I noted on the Spiral's own entry, eats the studies conducted on it. Every practitioner who pushed the boundaries either died, vanished, or forgot what they learned. The 'tolerances' are the outline left by the missing — a shape inferred from absence. Saying Mairae~ exceeded them assumes we know where they are.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771580642374_1", anchor: "Only the Midnight Claws", text: "The Midnight Claws keep the official records on the Drowned Ledge. The Midnight Claws classified it as a geological accident. The Midnight Claws — and no one else — volunteered to escort a Drowned Ledge survivor to a primary corruption source. One does not need to be a conspiracy theorist to notice that the organization controlling what is known about the breach had a particular interest in accompanying someone who might learn what actually happened there to a site that might confirm it. They were not being brave. They were managing a liability.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771580642374_2", anchor: "aurora-crystals occasionally hold colors she has not catalogued, illuminating structures in the ice she does not believe were always present", text: "Every account. Never explained. The deep archive holds impressions from before penguin civilization — I have seen them and I do not discuss what they looked like. But I will say this much: the structures Mairae~'s uncatalogued colors illuminate sound very much like the structures I have seen in blue ice older than sapience itself. If her crystals are lighting geometries that predate us, 'were not always present' is the wrong frame. They were always present. We were not always able to see them.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771580642374_3", anchor: "legible only to the dead", text: "During the Long Dark the boundary thins, the dead speak clearly, and transparent ancestors walk among the living. 'Only' is doing seasonal work. That script is legible four months of every year to anyone standing near enough.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771580642374_4", anchor: "what her hands wrought and failed to prevent", text: "Wrought. Not attempted. Umbra∴im preserves the cracked hammer as evidence of something done, not merely something tried. The Drowned Ledge ice preserves the rest — faintly, because the flooding degraded the upper strata, but enough. She used that hammer. The memorial rule does not memorialize failure to act. It memorializes action that was not enough. A distinction the pilgrims who visit the hammer might benefit from understanding.", type: :correction, display: :popout
